<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the ice hockey world</p>
<p>championship on Thursday:</p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>In Turku: Canada 5 United States 1 (1-0 1-0 3-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Canada - Rob Zamuner (01:22), Jeff Friesen (38:48), Anson</p>
<p>Carter (48:09), Owen Nolan (55:39) Travis Green (58:43)</p>
<p>United States - Ken Klee (50:22)</p>
<p>Penalties: Canada 16 minutes, United States 14</p>
<p>Attendance: 11,565</p>
<p>In Helsinki: Czech Republic 2 Russia 3 (2-1 0-1 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Czech Republic - Jiri Slegr (17:23), Pavel Patera (18:04)</p>
<p>Russia - Alexander Korolyuk (08:37), Denis Afinogenov</p>
<p>(26:21), Vyacheslav Butsayev (51:33).</p>
<p>Penalties: Czech Republic 16 minutes and Vladimir Vujtek 5</p>
<p>minutes (spearing) plus 20 minutes (misconduct), Russia 16</p>
<p>minutes</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,004</p>
